Making humans happy

2483
01:17:17,160 --> 01:17:19,320
is the greatest value
these animals have.

2484
01:17:20,500 --> 01:17:23,540
(Animals are killed once
they're no longer useful)

2485
01:17:23,580 --> 01:17:28,820
(Are animals here nothing
but products with no dignity?)

2486
01:17:29,120 --> 01:17:32,680
Maybe someone realized
the boss planned to discard them

2487
01:17:32,680 --> 01:17:34,240
and kill them.

2488
01:17:34,240 --> 01:17:36,200
Once he'd squeezed out all their value,

2489
01:17:36,200 --> 01:17:38,280
he'd have them killed.

2490
01:17:38,540 --> 01:17:41,740
(Theory: Someone heard the recording
and killed him in self-defense)

2491
01:17:42,040 --> 01:17:42,920
Have a seat.

2492
01:17:43,280 --> 01:17:44,360
Sit down. Go ahead.

2493
01:17:45,760 --> 01:17:47,160
We just found

2494
01:17:47,440 --> 01:17:48,520
that recording.

2495
01:17:48,920 --> 01:17:50,560
It said animals should be abused

2496
01:17:50,560 --> 01:17:52,000
because they're beasts, right?

2497
01:17:52,000 --> 01:17:52,560
Yes.

2498
01:17:52,560 --> 01:17:54,000
It also matches what Nan Shy

2499
01:17:54,480 --> 01:17:56,040
heard earlier.

2500
01:17:56,480 --> 01:17:58,200
(Toy bunny)
I heard something while grabbing it.

2501
01:17:58,200 --> 01:17:59,280
The boss was on the phone.

2502
01:18:00,600 --> 01:18:01,600
Judging by how he looks,

2503
01:18:01,600 --> 01:18:04,120
he's almost a full-on capybara.

2504
01:18:04,120 --> 01:18:07,120
Tomorrow, I'll send someone
tougher to fight him.

2505
01:18:07,120 --> 01:18:08,640
Let's see how long he lasts!

2506
01:18:09,960 --> 01:18:11,680
Those animals are just beasts.

2507
01:18:11,680 --> 01:18:13,760
Making us humans happy

2508
01:18:13,760 --> 01:18:16,560
is the greatest value they'll ever have.

2509
01:18:16,980 --> 01:18:20,780
(Both recordings point to animal abuse)

2510
01:18:21,240 --> 01:18:22,240
Okay, there are two more things.

2511
01:18:22,240 --> 01:18:23,240
What's the first one?

2512
01:18:23,240 --> 01:18:24,560
It's the Tui City Zoo

2513
01:18:24,560 --> 01:18:26,120
Operating Rules.

2514
01:18:26,400 --> 01:18:28,360
Star Animal Management Guidelines.

2515
01:18:28,360 --> 01:18:30,480
All animal handlers must follow them

2516
01:18:30,480 --> 01:18:32,520
to meet their assigned targets.

2517
01:18:32,800 --> 01:18:34,560
The face of the zoo

2518
01:18:34,560 --> 01:18:36,800
is Woofy, the celebrity dog.

2519
01:18:37,680 --> 01:18:39,640
(The face of the zoo)
As Tui City Zoo's biggest attraction,

2520
01:18:39,640 --> 01:18:41,240
Woofy must always maintain

2521
01:18:41,240 --> 01:18:42,800
a perfect public image.

2522
01:18:43,200 --> 01:18:44,280
Every day, he must complete

2523
01:18:44,280 --> 01:18:46,320
20 hours of livestream interaction.

2524
01:18:46,340 --> 01:18:49,700
(Woofy works 20 hours a day)

2525
01:18:49,880 --> 01:18:53,000
The aquarium's star beluga, Whaley.

2526
01:18:53,320 --> 01:18:54,200
(The aquarium's star)
Whaley.

2527
01:18:54,200 --> 01:18:56,880
She must perform ten water shows a day.

2528
01:18:57,560 --> 01:19:00,280
Every time she jumps from the water,

2529
01:19:00,280 --> 01:19:02,120
she must look graceful.

2530
01:19:02,560 --> 01:19:05,760
(Whaley performs in a cramped space)
Every move must be flawless.

2531
01:19:06,120 --> 01:19:07,280
Even if she's unwell,

2532
01:19:07,280 --> 01:19:09,760
she's never allowed to refuse.

2533
01:19:09,980 --> 01:19:11,780
(Whaley faces harsh conditions
and can't rest when sick)

2534
01:19:12,240 --> 01:19:13,880
Capy the capybara.

2535
01:19:14,120 --> 01:19:17,560
(Teasing room)
He stays calm with visitors.

2536
01:19:18,440 --> 01:19:21,440
Visitors can play any prank on Capy

2537
01:19:21,440 --> 01:19:22,080
or tease him

2538
01:19:22,480 --> 01:19:23,800
to prove

2539
01:19:23,800 --> 01:19:25,760
he'll never get angry.

2540
01:19:26,080 --> 01:19:27,920
That's basically an obedience test.

2541
01:19:27,980 --> 01:19:28,720
(Capy is bullied by visitors
and can't fight back)

2542
01:19:28,720 --> 01:19:29,800
I feel bad for you.

2543
01:19:31,600 --> 01:19:33,200
Bunbun the rabbit.

2544
01:19:33,200 --> 01:19:36,840
(Pet interaction zone)
She poses, shakes hands, and takes food.

2545
01:19:36,840 --> 01:19:39,920
If the rabbit becomes aggressive,

2546
01:19:39,920 --> 01:19:42,720
use electric shocks immediately.

2547
01:19:44,320 --> 01:19:47,120
If she scratches a visitor
out of instinctive fear,

2548
01:19:47,120 --> 01:19:49,520
(Fictional story with horror elements)
her claws must be forcibly filed down

2549
01:19:49,520 --> 01:19:52,080
without anesthesia.

2550
01:19:53,840 --> 01:19:55,360
So those claws are...

2551
01:19:55,780 --> 01:19:57,220
(Bunbun is shocked and has her claws
removed if she hurts someone)

2552
01:19:57,220 --> 01:19:58,580
(But her claws grow quickly,
so she wouldn't notice easily)

2553
01:19:59,040 --> 01:20:00,440
What about the other animals?

2554
01:20:00,840 --> 01:20:02,360
The wolf and fox exhibits.

2555
01:20:02,640 --> 01:20:03,320
You and I.

2556
01:20:03,320 --> 01:20:04,400
Ours too.

2557
01:20:04,400 --> 01:20:07,120
(Other animal areas)
For better visitor experience,

2558
01:20:07,120 --> 01:20:10,560
animals may be fed
human food by visitors.

2559
01:20:10,560 --> 01:20:11,760
If animals suffer from diarrhoea,

2560
01:20:11,760 --> 01:20:13,560
it is considered a minor issue

2561
01:20:13,560 --> 01:20:14,560
and there is no need
for excessive concern.

2562
01:20:15,200 --> 01:20:16,720
(Wolves and foxes may be freely fed)
We had diarrhoea all day yesterday.

2563
01:20:17,000 --> 01:20:18,400
(Diarrhoea is ignored)
So we just ate too much.

2564
01:20:19,280 --> 01:20:20,560
No, it was because of what
the visitors threw at us.

2565
01:20:20,560 --> 01:20:22,000
Most of those things
aren't suitable for us to eat.

2566
01:20:22,000 --> 01:20:23,280
For example, they gave us...

2567
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:24,800
hot and sour vermicelli,

2568
01:20:24,820 --> 01:20:26,580
(You were really hungry, huh?)

2569
01:20:27,000 --> 01:20:27,920
Stinky rice noodles.

2570
01:20:28,160 --> 01:20:28,960
Stinky tofu

2571
01:20:28,960 --> 01:20:30,760
or even hotpot soup base.

2572
01:20:31,040 --> 01:20:31,880
You two ate all of that?

2573
01:20:32,320 --> 01:20:33,600
(Two greedy little animals)
Don't you know what you can

2574
01:20:33,600 --> 01:20:34,600
and cannot eat?

2575
01:20:34,600 --> 01:20:36,560
Because it was given by visitors,

2576
01:20:36,560 --> 01:20:37,440
it made them feel good,

2577
01:20:37,440 --> 01:20:38,680
so we had to eat it.

2578
01:20:39,240 --> 01:20:40,840
(Customer comes first)
And we ended up with diarrhoea.

2579
01:20:41,860 --> 01:20:44,260
(Still too heavy and spicy)

2580
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:47,080
So we're actually in a zoo?

2581
01:20:49,420 --> 01:20:50,140
(Caring talent park)

2582
01:20:50,140 --> 01:20:51,780
(Is the game area actually a zoo?)

2583
01:20:52,000 --> 01:20:53,320
Yes, it's a zoo.

2584
01:20:53,320 --> 01:20:54,800
We're star animals.

2585
01:20:55,180 --> 01:20:58,500
(The six employees
are animals in the zoo?)

2586
01:20:58,800 --> 01:21:00,120
We thought we were humans, right?

2587
01:21:00,120 --> 01:21:01,440
We thought we were stars.

2588
01:21:01,440 --> 01:21:03,480
Turns out we're star animals.

2589
01:21:05,240 --> 01:21:06,840
Wait, look.

2590
01:21:08,240 --> 01:21:10,240
Does this look like my sister?

2591
01:21:11,700 --> 01:21:12,620
(Beluga whale)

2592
01:21:12,640 --> 01:21:14,080
They're identical.

2593
01:21:14,080 --> 01:21:15,320
Way too similar.

2594
01:21:16,240 --> 01:21:16,800
Yes.

2595
01:21:17,480 --> 01:21:18,320
Isn't it pretty?

2596
01:21:19,200 --> 01:21:20,360
Isn't it fair-skinned?

2597
01:21:20,500 --> 01:21:22,260
(No way to argue)

2598
01:21:23,600 --> 01:21:24,520
Anyway,

2599
01:21:24,520 --> 01:21:25,760
these six animals

2600
01:21:25,760 --> 01:21:27,440
represent the six of us.

2601
01:21:27,440 --> 01:21:28,080
Exactly.

2602
01:21:28,360 --> 01:21:29,960
Are we humans or animals?

2603
01:21:30,100 --> 01:21:31,660
(Are the six employees
humans or animals?)

2604
01:21:32,120 --> 01:21:32,480
No.

2605
01:21:33,200 --> 01:21:33,760
No,

2606
01:21:33,760 --> 01:21:34,840
humans are animals too.

2607
01:21:34,900 --> 01:21:37,260
(Humans are animals too,
Ke: I'm under too much pressure)

2608
01:21:37,280 --> 01:21:38,240
Uh,

2609
01:21:38,240 --> 01:21:39,640
they're playing with our minds now.

2610
01:21:40,060 --> 01:21:42,820
(Philosophical doggo)

2611
01:21:42,840 --> 01:21:44,120
We must be animals.

2612
01:21:44,360 --> 01:21:45,520
Why?

2613
01:21:45,520 --> 01:21:48,040
Because the words on our arms say

2614
01:21:48,040 --> 01:21:49,960
"revenge against humans."

2615
01:21:50,240 --> 01:21:50,720
It can't be humans

2616
01:21:50,720 --> 01:21:52,640
taking revenge on humans.

2617
01:21:52,640 --> 01:21:54,240
It must be animals

2618
01:21:54,240 --> 01:21:54,800
taking revenge on humans.

2619
01:21:54,800 --> 01:21:55,880
So maybe our minds,

2620
01:21:55,880 --> 01:21:56,760
or even

2621
01:21:56,760 --> 01:21:57,960
our true selves,

2622
01:21:57,960 --> 01:21:58,800
are actually animals.

2623
01:21:59,560 --> 01:21:59,960
Exactly.

2624
01:21:59,960 --> 01:22:03,900
(The theory: They were animals who
slowly gained human consciousness.)

2625
01:22:04,240 --> 01:22:05,440
There's a question we
need to solve today.

2626
01:22:05,440 --> 01:22:07,480
We need to figure out

2627
01:22:07,480 --> 01:22:09,120
the motives of the four suspects.

2628
01:22:09,180 --> 01:22:10,940
(Crime motive)

2629
01:22:11,600 --> 01:22:13,120
I don't have any motive.

2630
01:22:13,180 --> 01:22:14,300
(Motive completely denied?)

2631
01:22:14,600 --> 01:22:16,280
Too quick, bro.

2632
01:22:16,480 --> 01:22:18,200
(Does the detective think I'm harmless?)
You don't have a motive?

2633
01:22:18,800 --> 01:22:19,480
Sorry, just kidding.

2634
01:22:19,480 --> 01:22:20,040
I was joking.

2635
01:22:20,040 --> 01:22:20,880
Sorry.

2636
01:22:21,240 --> 01:22:22,880
(I for introvert, socially anxious)
Because you're introverted.

2637
01:22:22,880 --> 01:22:24,080
(Forced to livestream)
Then he forced you to livestream,

2638
01:22:24,080 --> 01:22:25,560
(Miserable)
making you suffer even more.

2639
01:22:25,580 --> 01:22:26,440
(All motives found)

2640
01:22:26,440 --> 01:22:26,880
Alright.

2641
01:22:27,200 --> 01:22:29,440
We remember everything clearly.

2642
01:22:30,080 --> 01:22:32,240
There's someone
smart sitting beside him.

2643
01:22:32,240 --> 01:22:33,800
You're done for, I'm telling you.

2644
01:22:33,900 --> 01:22:35,940
(Rabbit with internet memory)

2645
01:22:38,740 --> 01:22:41,700
(No way to defend himself)

2646
01:22:42,160 --> 01:22:44,080
(Unable to defend himself)

2647
01:22:44,840 --> 01:22:45,240
He can't explain himself anymore.

2648
01:22:45,240 --> 01:22:47,580
Alright.

2649
01:22:47,880 --> 01:22:50,040
(System crashed)

2650
01:22:50,040 --> 01:22:53,000
(Ke‘s motive: 1. Forced to livestream)
First, he forced you to livestream.

2651
01:22:53,000 --> 01:22:54,520
Second, because your sister
kept performing,

2652
01:22:54,520 --> 01:22:55,200
you wanted to take her away

2653
01:22:55,200 --> 01:22:57,000
and escape from here.

2654
01:22:57,000 --> 01:22:57,360
(2. Failed escape with Jin Goofy)
But you failed to escape.

2655
01:22:57,380 --> 01:22:58,420
Right?

2656
01:22:58,420 --> 01:22:59,460
(Ke Uh-Oh's motive summary:
1. Forced to livestream)

2657
01:22:59,480 --> 01:23:01,200
(2. Wanted to escape
the park with Jin Goofy)

2658
01:23:01,920 --> 01:23:04,920
What about you, Little Fish?

2659
01:23:04,920 --> 01:23:06,440
I think first,
he made me feel exhausted.

2660
01:23:06,440 --> 01:23:07,480
He kept forcing me to perform.

2661
01:23:07,480 --> 01:23:09,520
(Jin Goofy's motive summary:)
I truly started wanting to kill him

2662
01:23:09,520 --> 01:23:11,580
(1. Forced to perform)
when he hurt my brother.

2663
01:23:11,600 --> 01:23:13,520
(2. Found his brother was abused)
So I had

2664
01:23:13,520 --> 01:23:15,400
to save him at all costs.

2665
01:23:15,800 --> 01:23:17,640
Your new movie
is coming out soon, right?

2666
01:23:17,640 --> 01:23:18,520
No.

2667
01:23:18,880 --> 01:23:20,560
Before that, I had to eliminate

2668
01:23:20,560 --> 01:23:21,640
everyone controlling you.

2669
01:23:21,640 --> 01:23:23,120
(Big motive)
Right. I had to leave for promotions.

2670
01:23:23,600 --> 01:23:25,000
So you killed him?

2671
01:23:25,200 --> 01:23:25,720
Yes, I had no time.

2672
01:23:25,720 --> 01:23:26,640
I had to escape.

2673
01:23:28,080 --> 01:23:29,920
Alright,
what about Little Bunny's motive?

2674
01:23:30,160 --> 01:23:30,640
My motive?

2675
01:23:30,640 --> 01:23:31,520
I don't have one.

2676
01:23:31,980 --> 01:23:33,020
(No way)
Hmph.

2677
01:23:33,430 --> 01:23:34,260
Hmph.

2678
01:23:34,520 --> 01:23:35,920
You're learning fast, baby.

2679
01:23:36,460 --> 01:23:38,100
(Just adapting)

2680
01:23:38,200 --> 01:23:38,960
No motive.

2681
01:23:40,040 --> 01:23:41,800
(Let the family help)
Come on, let your boyfriend accuse her.

2682
01:23:41,800 --> 01:23:42,920
What was her motive?

2683
01:23:42,920 --> 01:23:43,400
Right.

2684
01:23:44,060 --> 01:23:45,900
(I won't speak until my partner does)

2685
01:23:46,280 --> 01:23:47,880
We have no motive at all.

2686
01:23:47,880 --> 01:23:49,400
(Defending together)
We're just kind-hearted

2687
01:23:49,400 --> 01:23:50,800
and easygoing.

2688
01:23:50,800 --> 01:23:52,160
(You can't fool this detective)
Because you were too nice

2689
01:23:52,160 --> 01:23:53,120
and finally snapped.

2690
01:23:53,120 --> 01:23:53,840
Yes.

2691
01:23:54,440 --> 01:23:56,160
(Detective takes control)
What is Nan's motive?

2692
01:23:56,640 --> 01:23:57,640
Nan's first motive is...

2693
01:23:58,040 --> 01:23:59,080
Pulling out her nails.

2694
01:23:59,320 --> 01:24:01,080
(Nan's motive summary:)
Nail removal and electric shocks, right?

2695
01:24:01,080 --> 01:24:02,160
(1. Abused by the boss)
She was truly being abused.

2696
01:24:02,160 --> 01:24:02,400
Yes,

2697
01:24:02,400 --> 01:24:02,760
abuse.

2698
01:24:02,760 --> 01:24:03,360
It was abuse.

2699
01:24:03,360 --> 01:24:03,680
Yeah.

2700
01:24:03,680 --> 01:24:05,840
And she also noticed
her boyfriend was slowly...

2701
01:24:05,840 --> 01:24:06,760
Getting worse.

2702
01:24:07,060 --> 01:24:07,800
(Did I say that right?)

2703
01:24:07,800 --> 01:24:09,520
Turning into a capybara.

2704
01:24:09,520 --> 01:24:11,080
Her boyfriend was in danger.

2705
01:24:11,100 --> 01:24:11,760
(Nan's motive summary:)

2706
01:24:11,760 --> 01:24:12,200
(1. Abused by the boss)
Alright.

2707
01:24:12,200 --> 01:24:12,960
(2. Realized He Struggle was in danger)

2708
01:24:12,960 --> 01:24:14,640
So her motive is valid.

2709
01:24:14,640 --> 01:24:15,080
Valid.

2710
01:24:15,560 --> 01:24:18,000
You're quick to push this onto me.

2711
01:24:19,040 --> 01:24:20,320
No, I'm not.

2712
01:24:20,800 --> 01:24:22,480
Alright, what about him?

2713
01:24:22,480 --> 01:24:23,600
What about Little Ka?

2714
01:24:23,800 --> 01:24:25,200
My emotional logic is this:

2715
01:24:25,200 --> 01:24:26,800
I was constantly being abused,

2716
01:24:26,800 --> 01:24:27,760
but my personality

2717
01:24:27,760 --> 01:24:28,880
wouldn't let me

2718
01:24:28,880 --> 01:24:30,120
feel extremely wronged.

2719
01:24:30,120 --> 01:24:31,360
A giant in spirit,

2720
01:24:31,360 --> 01:24:32,620
but weak in action.

2721
01:24:33,320 --> 01:24:35,560
But what really affected me

2722
01:24:35,560 --> 01:24:37,000
was seeing my partner

2723
01:24:37,480 --> 01:24:38,480
feel sorry for what I was going through.

2724
01:24:38,480 --> 01:24:40,000
Seeing how heartbroken

2725
01:24:40,000 --> 01:24:41,920
she was because she cared about me.

2726
01:24:41,920 --> 01:24:44,160
I ended up feeling sorry
for both her and myself.

2727
01:24:44,920 --> 01:24:48,520
(Love excuse, two birds with one stone)
He really said everything possible.

2728
01:24:48,840 --> 01:24:50,520
You said it all.

2729
01:24:50,620 --> 01:24:52,240
(Rambling)

2730
01:24:52,240 --> 01:24:53,840
(Singles can't handle this)
I get it. You don't need to continue.

2731
01:24:53,840 --> 01:24:54,920
I feel sorry for your partner.

2732
01:24:57,040 --> 01:24:59,440
My capybara personality

2733
01:24:59,440 --> 01:25:01,160
is naturally harmless.

2734
01:25:01,160 --> 01:25:02,080
(Emotionally stable)
I could never do anything

2735
01:25:02,080 --> 01:25:03,480
(Harmless to humans)
to hurt people.

2736
01:25:03,480 --> 01:25:03,960
(Super kind Little Ka)
Exactly.

2737
01:25:03,960 --> 01:25:04,360
Makes sense.

2738
01:25:04,360 --> 01:25:05,600
But even so,

2739
01:25:05,600 --> 01:25:07,840
seeing someone who cares
about me being hurt

2740
01:25:07,840 --> 01:25:09,360
(Bold deduction!)
makes me feel...

2741
01:25:09,680 --> 01:25:10,800
Feel upset.

2742
01:25:11,080 --> 01:25:12,760
You can leave now, friend.

2743
01:25:13,280 --> 01:25:14,240
That's just who I am.

2744
01:25:16,680 --> 01:25:17,720
And then you saw

2745
01:25:17,720 --> 01:25:19,760
the person you love being hurt...

2746
01:25:19,760 --> 01:25:21,000
Being abused.

2747
01:25:21,000 --> 01:25:22,240
Did you want to kill the boss?

2748
01:25:23,000 --> 01:25:24,200
I wanted to.

2749
01:25:24,200 --> 01:25:25,240
But I didn't dare.

2750
01:25:25,600 --> 01:25:27,040
Do I look like someone who could?

2751
01:25:27,060 --> 01:25:28,220
(Coward! Got it?)

2752
01:25:28,520 --> 01:25:28,880
Yes.

2753
01:25:30,760 --> 01:25:32,360
(Wolf King reenactment)
Would I dare?

2754
01:25:36,580 --> 01:25:39,620
(He Struggle's motive analysis:
Girlfriend abused by her boss)

2755
01:25:40,120 --> 01:25:41,600
So based on this,

2756
01:25:41,600 --> 01:25:42,640
your motive for murder

2757
01:25:42,640 --> 01:25:43,480
is clear.

2758
01:25:43,800 --> 01:25:44,680
But now we face

2759
01:25:44,680 --> 01:25:46,920
a terrifying problem.

2760
01:25:47,520 --> 01:25:48,000
What is it?

2761
01:25:51,080 --> 01:25:52,560
The time of death.

2762
01:25:53,240 --> 01:25:54,400
We simply can't determine it.

2763
01:25:55,240 --> 01:25:55,800
Yeah.

2764
01:25:55,800 --> 01:25:56,200
Exactly.

2765
01:25:56,200 --> 01:25:59,140
(Unable to determine the key point,
time of death)

2766
01:25:59,160 --> 01:25:59,920
Think about it.

2767
01:25:59,920 --> 01:26:00,840
Before the meeting,

2768
01:26:00,840 --> 01:26:02,880
the boss came out to give a speech.

2769
01:26:03,200 --> 01:26:03,680
He sat down,

2770
01:26:03,680 --> 01:26:05,120
and just as everyone
was preparing to start the party...

2771
01:26:05,480 --> 01:26:06,240
(Boss starts the ghost story session)
Thanks for coming.

2772
01:26:06,240 --> 01:26:08,640
our crazy animal theme party.

2773
01:26:09,000 --> 01:26:12,120
Our first thrilling segment,

2774
01:26:12,120 --> 01:26:13,960
the City Ghost Story Sharing Session,

2775
01:26:13,960 --> 01:26:15,040
begins now.

2776
01:26:15,840 --> 01:26:16,840
After he finished speaking and left,

2777
01:26:16,840 --> 01:26:18,160
we continued with the party.

2778
01:26:18,600 --> 01:26:19,600
Suddenly, the power went out.

2779
01:26:19,600 --> 01:26:21,720
And the boss's body appeared.

2780
01:26:21,880 --> 01:26:24,080
(Timeline analysis)
Actually, we do know the time of death.

2781
01:26:24,560 --> 01:26:25,760
(2:30PM, Boss's speech)
So from the moment he left.

2782
01:26:26,280 --> 01:26:28,120
(Animals' sharing session)
until his leg fell.

2783
01:26:28,720 --> 01:26:30,800
(Boss's body discovered)
Before we entered the lockers,

2784
01:26:30,800 --> 01:26:32,400
(Time of death: 2:30PM to ?)
his torso had already appeared.

2785
01:26:32,800 --> 01:26:34,560
(The six animals enter the lockers)
So all of us had...

2786
01:26:34,560 --> 01:26:35,360
(The boss died before
anyone could act alone)

2787
01:26:35,360 --> 01:26:36,520
An alibi.

2788
01:26:36,520 --> 01:26:38,000
Right, an alibi.

2789
01:26:38,020 --> 01:26:42,500
(Everyone has an alibi?)

2790
01:26:42,520 --> 01:26:45,040
How could he do it

2791
01:26:45,040 --> 01:26:46,400
while staying with us the whole time?

2792
01:26:46,400 --> 01:26:48,360
And even leave the leg at the scene?

2793
01:26:48,380 --> 01:26:52,100
(How was the boss killed
and dismembered in plain sight?)

2794
01:26:52,680 --> 01:26:54,720
I think there's one possibility,
an accomplice.

2795
01:26:54,720 --> 01:26:55,080
Right?

2796
01:26:55,080 --> 01:26:57,180
(Could the killer
have had an accomplice?)

2797
01:26:57,200 --> 01:26:59,360
Exactly, there had to be a third person.

2798
01:26:59,360 --> 01:27:00,840
Secretary Tui.

2799
01:27:01,360 --> 01:27:03,200
(Secretary: Bu Kakao by Li Bangbang)
They're all company employees.

2800
01:27:03,520 --> 01:27:05,360
(VIP Client: Tai Kule by Tai Wei)
So you do know I'm your top client.

2801
01:27:05,360 --> 01:27:06,480
The computer belongs to Duo Ge too.

2802
01:27:06,760 --> 01:27:08,240
Who's Duo Ge? The receptionist?

2803
01:27:08,240 --> 01:27:09,040
No idea.

2804
01:27:09,100 --> 01:27:10,340
(Tui Games Company: Duo Ge)

2805
01:27:10,340 --> 01:27:12,140
(Could one of them be the accomplice?)

2806
01:27:12,160 --> 01:27:14,160
The method of murder is something
we still have no idea about.

2807
01:27:14,880 --> 01:27:15,720
Absolutely no idea.

2808
01:27:15,880 --> 01:27:17,960
Then what was the cause of his death?

2809
01:27:18,020 --> 01:27:19,400
(Starting from the cause of death)

2810
01:27:19,400 --> 01:27:20,480
As for the cause of his death,

2811
01:27:20,480 --> 01:27:22,160
I think it is very likely

2812
01:27:22,160 --> 01:27:23,520
that he had already lost consciousness

2813
01:27:23,520 --> 01:27:25,360
before he died.

2814
01:27:25,800 --> 01:27:27,400
(Victim unconscious before death)
He couldn't stay conscious.

2815
01:27:27,400 --> 01:27:29,000
and endure the pain
of being dismembered,

2816
01:27:29,000 --> 01:27:30,520
while their body was left to rot

2817
01:27:30,520 --> 01:27:32,120
inside water.

2818
01:27:32,360 --> 01:27:33,680
But the problem is,

2819
01:27:33,680 --> 01:27:35,120
we only found one poison.

2820
01:27:35,120 --> 01:27:36,840
(Melt-Away, corrosive dissolving liquid)
It's called Melt-Away.

2821
01:27:36,840 --> 01:27:38,000
This only has

2822
01:27:38,000 --> 01:27:38,920
a dissolving effect.

2823
01:27:38,920 --> 01:27:39,720
It doesn't have any effect

2824
01:27:39,720 --> 01:27:41,080
that causes someone
to lose consciousness.

2825
01:27:41,080 --> 01:27:42,840
(How did the victim lose consciousness
before being dismembered?)

2826
01:27:42,840 --> 01:27:44,600
We know the time of death.

2827
01:27:44,600 --> 01:27:45,760
It was between the moment he left

2828
01:27:45,760 --> 01:27:47,520
and the moment his leg fell down.

2829
01:27:47,520 --> 01:27:48,880
When he died,

2830
01:27:48,880 --> 01:27:50,680
he must have already been unconscious.

2831
01:27:52,520 --> 01:27:54,400
Did you notice his head earlier?

2832
01:27:54,960 --> 01:27:56,120
(The victim's head?)
What happened to his head?

2833
01:27:56,120 --> 01:27:58,120
His head actually doesn't look like...

2834
01:27:58,960 --> 01:27:59,600
Doesn't look like what?

2835
01:28:02,920 --> 01:28:04,320
Like he was electrocuted.

2836
01:28:04,320 --> 01:28:06,000
Like he was electrocuted?

2837
01:28:07,880 --> 01:28:08,960
Where did you see that?

2838
01:28:09,460 --> 01:28:10,280
(Story setting:
Contains fictional horror elements)

2839
01:28:10,280 --> 01:28:11,280
This is the boss's head.

2840
01:28:14,100 --> 01:28:16,060
(Burn marks)

2841
01:28:16,360 --> 01:28:17,840
It had burn marks and blackened areas.

2842
01:28:18,240 --> 01:28:18,600
Where?

2843
01:28:19,080 --> 01:28:19,920
On his face.

2844
01:28:20,500 --> 01:28:23,460
(Ding Staring Speculation: Victim lost
consciousness from electrocution)

2845
01:28:23,480 --> 01:28:25,640
I noticed there were no marks
on his hands.

2846
01:28:25,800 --> 01:28:26,440
None on his hands?

2847
01:28:26,440 --> 01:28:27,080
Right.

2848
01:28:27,140 --> 01:28:28,220
(Clue: Why are there burns
on the head but not the limbs?)

2849
01:28:28,220 --> 01:28:30,140
(Story setting:
Contains fictional horror elements)

2850
01:28:30,720 --> 01:28:31,920
I think we should consider

2851
01:28:31,920 --> 01:28:34,080
why did he use Melt-Away?

2852
01:28:34,480 --> 01:28:34,960
Yeah, why?

2853
01:28:34,960 --> 01:28:35,280
Exactly.

2854
01:28:35,280 --> 01:28:38,100
(Speculation: Why did the killer
use Melt-Away to destroy the body?)

2855
01:28:38,400 --> 01:28:40,240
I think he wanted to destroy something.

2856
01:28:41,040 --> 01:28:41,480
Right.

2857
01:28:41,480 --> 01:28:42,160
The question is,

2858
01:28:42,160 --> 01:28:43,880
why did he only dissolve...

2859
01:28:44,160 --> 01:28:44,800
The torso.

2860
01:28:44,800 --> 01:28:45,880
Right. The hands and other...

2861
01:28:45,880 --> 01:28:46,680
Other limbs.

2862
01:28:46,680 --> 01:28:47,720
Yes, why leave the hands
and limbs behind?

2863
01:28:48,060 --> 01:28:51,700
(Speculation: Why did the killer
only dissolve the victim's torso?)

2864
01:28:51,700 --> 01:28:54,860
(Story setting:
Contains fictional horror elements)

2865
01:29:12,620 --> 01:29:14,020
(Next Episode Preview:
Trading Places, Blood for Blood)

2866
01:29:17,240 --> 01:29:18,360
What kind of place is this?

2867
01:29:18,680 --> 01:29:20,280
They claim to love us,

2868
01:29:20,280 --> 01:29:22,920
yet use that love to imprison us.

2869
01:29:22,920 --> 01:29:23,640
And some humans

2870
01:29:23,640 --> 01:29:25,920
even hurt

2871
01:29:25,920 --> 01:29:27,920
and abuse our kind.

2872
01:29:27,920 --> 01:29:28,680
I'll kill him.

2873
01:29:28,680 --> 01:29:31,440
I'll make you villains
feel the same pain.

2874
01:29:31,440 --> 01:29:33,480
Revenge.

2875
01:29:33,480 --> 01:29:34,440
Kill him.

2876
01:29:34,440 --> 01:29:34,960
Kill him!

2877
01:29:36,480 --> 01:29:37,400
We were injected with

2878
01:29:37,400 --> 01:29:38,520
a human transformation serum.

2879
01:29:38,520 --> 01:29:40,040
They turned us into them.

2880
01:29:40,040 --> 01:29:41,280
So we could experience their suffering.

2881
01:29:41,280 --> 01:29:43,080
We've already lost our human dignity.

2882
01:29:45,180 --> 01:29:45,900
(Little Ka)

2883
01:29:45,920 --> 01:29:46,880
Animal gravestones.

2884
01:29:46,880 --> 01:29:48,280
Are we already dead?

2885
01:29:48,280 --> 01:29:49,640
Then what are we now?

2886
01:29:49,640 --> 01:29:50,800
(The Sin of Hypocrisy Revealed)

2887
01:29:50,800 --> 01:29:52,960
They say rabbits can endure pain well.

2888
01:29:53,680 --> 01:29:54,880
I can't watch this anymore.

2889
01:29:54,880 --> 01:29:55,480
It's so cruel.

2890
01:29:55,480 --> 01:29:56,640
They turned us into this

2891
01:29:56,640 --> 01:29:58,040
and abused us again.

2892
01:30:00,680 --> 01:30:02,280
He wants revenge for these animals.

2893
01:30:02,280 --> 01:30:05,600
But what right does he
have to kill Tui Haowan?

2894
01:30:05,600 --> 01:30:06,280
(Beneath the Masks,
Humans Devouring Each Other)

2895
01:30:06,280 --> 01:30:07,680
The most exciting part is here.

2896
01:30:07,680 --> 01:30:09,480
We can tear each other apart now.

2897
01:30:09,480 --> 01:30:10,680
You seem like the killer.

2898
01:30:10,680 --> 01:30:12,920
I'm only at home in water.

2899
01:30:12,920 --> 01:30:14,480
That's a stretch.

2900
01:30:14,480 --> 01:30:15,840
You're more like the boss.

2901
01:30:15,840 --> 01:30:16,760
Rabbit family.

2902
01:30:16,760 --> 01:30:18,160
(Rabbit Family)
They have excellent night vision.

2903
01:30:18,160 --> 01:30:18,840
You don't believe me?

2904
01:30:18,840 --> 01:30:19,840
There's no room for sympathy here.

2905
01:30:19,840 --> 01:30:20,960
I believe my younger brother

2906
01:30:20,960 --> 01:30:22,600
